Z||000000||350ZZ4||07-09-2000||06:40 AM||||It never ceases, it just whines constantly, its like a buzzing hum clearly audible from the interior. Should I just replace it ASAP? How much labour is involved? ||||reg||1
Z||000001||Vader||07-09-2000||09:12 AM||||350,<P>I've had a "squealer" in my '84 SE for about six years now.  It makes more than enough pressure and flow.  It tends to get a little more annoying when the tank is less than half-full, and quiets to a low "whimper" in a full tank.  I've been waiting for it to die so I'll have an excuse to do some other mods in preparation for a 355 SBC swap (larger pump), but it keeps on pumping.  <P>It can last a long time that way or fail tomorrow.  There's just no really good way to tell.  As long as pressure and flow are adequate, and the noise doesn't change rapidly over the next few days, it might survive.  Still, it would be a good idea to scan the manual and familiarized yourself with the replacement procedure, and maybe find a source for a replacement pump - just in case.<P>Later,<BR>Vader<P>------------------<BR>"<I>Make Me Bad</I>"||||reg||1
